A //plumb: directive on an alias to an anonymous struct is a valid whole-struct
provider: only an alias whose target is not a struct is rejected, and this one is
a struct. plumb builds the composite literal naming the alias (S{...}) and
resolves the field as an input.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

//plumb:build
type S = struct{ X int }

//plumb:build
func provideX() int { return 5 }

//plumb:build
func use(s S) string { return "" }
